# AGENTS.md

Context for any coding agent working on this project. Read this before changing anything.

All three Sortie prompts read this file — the planning stage plans against it, the build
stage treats it as binding, and the review stage checks the work against it. It is the one
place to encode what an agent cannot infer from the code in the time it has. Delete the
guidance in brackets as you fill each section in.

## What this is

[One or two paragraphs. What the project does and who it is for. Point at the deeper
explanation — `README.md`, a design doc — rather than repeating it.]

## Hard constraints

[The rules that are load-bearing: a change breaking one is wrong even if it works. Be
specific and say why, so the agent can recognise a novel case. Typical entries:

- Dependency policy — what may be added, and what must never be.
- Language or runtime floor, and the syntax it rules out.
- Anything with real-world side effects that the code must not do.
- Invariants that look like implementation detail but are deliberate.
- Things CI greps for and will reject.]

